# Stage4 LIVE-ONLY package list — Orange Pi 4 LTS (arm64).
# One atom per line; lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Appended by build-orangepi4-lts-stage4.sh ONLY when the LIVE flavor is being
# built (BUILD_LIVE=true: --flavor live | both). The LIVE flavor boots a
# squashfs rootfs ephemerally; that requires a dracut dmsquash-live initramfs
# to find the live medium, mount LiveOS/squashfs.img read-only, and stack a
# writable tmpfs overlay as the ephemeral root. The bare kernel canNOT
# interpret root=live: / rd.live.* on its own — those are dracut directives —
# so dracut must be present in the cross sysroot to GENERATE that initramfs at
# build time. Mirrors specs-frite/portage/packages-live.list exactly.
#
# The INSTALLER flavor's OWN medium is ALSO a live boot (see the builder's
# build_installer_iso — same as Frite), so dracut is needed whenever EITHER
# bootable flavor is selected; it stays out of the always-installed base set
# and is added here.

# dracut: builds the dmsquash-live initramfs (and, for --encrypt-root, the
# separate disk-boot crypt-capable initramfs). The builder invokes it as a host
# tool pointed at the aarch64 sysroot (qemu-chroot preferred; see the builder).
sys-kernel/dracut
